    "faq.6.q": "Why do member numbers matter?",
    "faq.6.a": "The Labour Code ties a union's representativeness to its membership: once at least 10% of an employer's workforce is unionised, the union is entitled to conclude a collective agreement.",
    "about.mission.more": "Under the Fundamental Law of Hungary, trade unions protect and represent employees' interests, using the rights set out in the Labour Code. Our union carries out both representative and service activities. Its main powers are concluding collective agreements and negotiating pay and benefits with the employer.",
    "about.org.t": "Our structure",
    "about.org.title": "An organisation built <em>from the ground up</em>.",
    "about.org.1.t": "Members",
    "about.org.1.d": "They form union groups and elect a shop steward from among themselves.",
    "about.org.2.t": "Shop stewards",
    "about.org.2.d": "In each area they elect a chief shop steward from among themselves.",
    "about.org.3.t": "Chief shop stewards",
    "about.org.3.d": "They sit on the Council. Where there is no chief steward, the group's shop steward sits on it directly.",
    "about.org.core.k": "Highest decision-making body",
    "about.org.core.t": "Stewards' Council (FBT)",
    "about.org.core.d": "The Council elects the members of the Union Committee and the senior officers for 5 years.",
    "about.org.4.t": "Union Committee (SZB)",
    "about.org.4.d": "The union's administrative body. Its members are elected by the Council for 5 years.",
    "about.org.5.t": "Senior officers",
